  "awb---key-feature-1-content": "<h3>Team Ridge beats Harbor by one answer</h3><p>Every Friday at 4:00, Larch Point Analytics splits its 24 analysts into 4 teams of 6 for a 10-question team quiz on a video call. The leaderboard updates after every question. Ridge finished on 8 correct, one ahead of Harbor at 7, with Summit on 6 and Delta on 5. Each answer is saved with the round it came from.</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Team Quiz Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What are some good team quiz ideas?\", \"a\": \"Good team quiz ideas mix rounds everyone can play: a picture round of office objects shot up close, a round matching teammates to their baby photos, a company history round, and one on the industry you work in. Finish with a number question as the tiebreaker, where the closest guess wins.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a team quiz?\", \"a\": \"Describe the occasion, the rounds, and how teams score, and Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder'>AI survey builder</a> builds the questions and answer keys, plus the leaderboard, from that prompt. Read every question before game day, change any of them by prompting, then send players one link.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can I make a free team quiz for my coworkers?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Emergent is free to start, and the free tier covers building and publishing. Publish the quiz and send the link to your coworkers. The team role quiz near the top of this page is also free to play, with no account and no email.\"}, {\"q\": \"How many team quiz questions should one round have?\", \"a\": \"Ten questions make a good round: enough to separate the teams, and short enough to finish in about 5 minutes on a call. Three rounds fill a 30-minute game with time for the reveals. When the goal is to hear how people feel about working together, send a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/team'>team survey</a> instead.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I write team quiz questions and answers nobody argues with?\", \"a\": \"Give each question one answer you can check, and note where you checked it. Avoid questions about the best or the biggest of anything, which invite more than one fair reply. For number questions, award the closest guess. Read the answer aloud at the reveal, and the dispute ends there.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you keep score in a team quiz on a video call?\", \"a\": \"Let each player answer on their own phone and count every correct answer as a point for their team. The app adds the points as answers come in and shows the standings on the shared screen after each question. A disputed point can be checked against the saved answer, which sits in a database you own.\"}, {\"q\": \"Does a team quiz help with team building at work?\", \"a\": \"It can, when teams mix people who rarely work together and the questions reward the group over one expert. Treat it as a shared half hour, not a measure of how people feel about their jobs. To measure that, run an <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/employee-engagement'>employee engagement survey</a> with its own questions.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a new hire quiz about the team ask?\", \"a\": \"Ask what a new hire needs in the first month: who approves what, which tool handles which task, and who to call after hours. Keep it to 8 questions and send each score to the manager. A missed question shows what to cover in the next one-on-one.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I run a team quiz for a remote team across time zones?\", \"a\": \"Pick an hour inside working time for every location and play it live, or leave the quiz open for 24 hours and rank teams on their total. The live game keeps one shared leaderboard, while the open window is fairer to distant offices. A quiz built on Emergent has no response cap, however many offices join.\"}, {\"q\": \"Should managers see individual team quiz scores?\", \"a\": \"For a game, no: show team totals and keep each player's score out of view. For a knowledge quiz, such as one for new hires, the manager can see the score when people know that up front. Feedback about the manager belongs in a separate <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-survey-and-quiz-builder/manager-feedback'>manager feedback survey</a>.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
